---
// SOURCE: zurp-astronomics-site — main site (v2) footer: the footer copy (jokes) on a black band
// AUTHOR: engineer
// DATE: 2026-10-03
// STATUS: active
// REVISED: 2026-10-06 (ticket #49) — every text comes from content/ (site.yml, footer/legalese.md)
//
// The copy began as the v1 footer's, word for word (v1 deleted in ticket #35), and lives in
// content/site.yml (`name`, `affiliation`, `signature`, `org`, `footer`) and content/footer/legalese.md: home line
// (the site's signature) without a product, product line with one.
// The "Low-Tech & DIY" panel (the worn version, src/assets/header/low-tech-diy-poster.webp) signs
// the footer of EVERY page of the main site, home included, small (~140 px, the size of the v1
// sticker). Ticket #14 had left it out of the home page (its header shows the same poster full
// size); the human found the gap odd, and ticket #16 put it back: do not reintroduce a condition on
// `productName` here, which only picks the footer's copy line. Variants at 140 and 280 px (1x / 2x)
// only: it is never displayed wider. Ticket #35 removed the "v1" link with the v1 archive it led to.
// Ticket #23: the panel is a link back to the top of the page (`#top`, the id on <body> in
// V2Layout.astro), with nothing visible added — no text, no icon: the human wanted it unannounced,
// the existing hover is the hint. Its accessible name is "Back to top" (aria-label), so it is not
// silent for screen readers. Smooth scroll comes from `scroll-behavior` on html.z2, already turned
// off under prefers-reduced-motion. No JavaScript. The footer is cut off from the page by ONE thin
// rule (the old 4 px red border + 2 px red echo doubled the signature's own red rules).
// `fit="outside"` (ticket #43, Astro 7): the panel is 3:2 (1536 × 1024) and 140 px gives a 93 px
// height, so Astro 7 asks for its 280 px variant at 280 × 186 (= 280 / (140 / 93)) and its image
// service CROPS to that by default. "outside" (sharp's fit: keep the ratio, cover the box) scales
// instead, as Astro 4 did: 280 × 187, the whole panel. `fit` never reaches the HTML.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import lowTechPoster from '../../assets/header/low-tech-diy-poster.webp';
import { fill, inlineMarkdown, readMarkdown, siteContent, siteView } from '../../lib/content.mjs';

interface Props {
  productName?: string;
}

const { productName } = Astro.props;

const site = siteContent();
const legalese = inlineMarkdown(readMarkdown('footer/legalese.md'));
---

<footer class="foot">
  <div class="z2-container foot-inner">
    <p class="z2-signature foot-sig" aria-hidden="true"><span>{site.name}</span></p>
    <p class="org-link">
      {site.footer.orgLabel} <a href={site.org.url}>{site.org.handle}</a>
    </p>
    {
      productName ? (
        <p>
          <em>{fill(site.footer.productLine, { ...siteView(site), product: productName })}</em>
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          <em>{site.signature}</em>
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p class="legalese" set:html={legalese} />
    <a class="lowtech-link" href="#top" aria-label={site.footer.backToTop}>
      <Image
        src={lowTechPoster}
        alt={site.footer.panelAlt}
        title={site.footer.panelTitle}
        width={140}
        widths={[140, 280]}
        fit="outside"
        sizes="140px"
        format="webp"
        quality={72}
        loading="lazy"
        class="lowtech-panel"
      />
    </a>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .foot {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 5rem;
    padding: 3.25rem 0 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05) 0 1px, transparent 1.6px) 0 0 / 5px 5px,
      var(--z2-soot-deep);
    /* One thin, quiet rule between the page and the footer, in the dimmed cream of the home
       page's hairline. The red belongs to the signature's two rules just below. */
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201, 187, 152, 0.35); /* --z2-cream-dim at 35 % */
  }

  .foot-inner {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .foot-sig {
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--z2-cream);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .foot p {
    color: var(--z2-cream-dim);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .foot .foot-sig {
    color: var(--z2-cream);
  }

  .org-link {
    font-family: var(--z2-font-type);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .org-link a {
    color: var(--z2-cream);
  }

  .legalese {
    font-size: 0.82rem !important;
  }

  /* The back-to-top link wraps the panel tightly, so the focus ring (html.z2 a:focus-visible)
     draws round it. */
  .lowtech-link {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 1.75rem auto 0;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* Footer signature, not a second poster: dimmed and slightly askew on the black band, it lights
     up and straightens a little on hover or keyboard focus (the v1 sticker's gesture, kept
     discreet) — the only hint that it is clickable. */
  .lowtech-panel {
    display: block;
    width: 140px;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 3px;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(236, 223, 191, 0.12), 0 6px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    opacity: 0.7;
    filter: saturate(0.85);
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease, filter 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .lowtech-link:hover .lowtech-panel,
  .lowtech-link:focus-visible .lowtech-panel {
    opacity: 1;
    filter: none;
    transform: scale(1.1) rotate(1deg);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .lowtech-panel,
    .lowtech-link:hover .lowtech-panel,
    .lowtech-link:focus-visible .lowtech-panel {
      transition: none;
      transform: rotate(-2deg);
    }
  }
</style>
